From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:46:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Athena API: say what now crosses world threads

Entities other than players move between worlds ticked by different threads,
vanilla commands run with every world thread waiting, and scoreboards and
hiding players may be used from any thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
index 232a061759e4ce02d281dd484b5265d52f90128a..c3b1becfa812d0dc7918fafb20a23f6b00f6bae8 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
@@ -418,8 +418,12 @@ public final class Athena {
      * different threads in two steps: it leaves on its old world's thread and arrives on the new
      * one's, so {@code teleport} returns before the player is there, and a player on the way cannot
      * be teleported again. A login aimed at such a world lands in the main world and is then moved.
-     * Entities other than players do not move between worlds ticked by different threads, and the
-     * main world cannot have its own thread.
+     * Other entities move the same way: written out and removed on the old world's thread, made again
+     * on the new one's (riders and leashes stay behind). The main world cannot have its own thread.
+     *
+     * <p>Vanilla commands then run on the server thread with every world thread waiting between two
+     * ticks, since they may touch any world; one typed in a world on its own thread runs a moment
+     * later. A scoreboard may be changed from any thread, and so may who hides whom.
      *
      * @throws IllegalStateException if {@code world} is the main world, or this is called from inside
      *         the world's own tick
